From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakefield kernel fixes <lakefield@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:08:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] i915: treat an unaccepted power-well request as an absent
 gate

Lakefield's PW_2 is fused off, and the hardware does not accept its
enable request at all: HSW_PWR_WELL_CTL_REQ() reads back 0 straight after
the write while the other wells set REQ and STATE. That currently ends in
a timeout WARN on every boot for a gate that can never come up.

Check whether the request bit stuck and, if it did not, log at debug
level and carry on. Do not use SKL_FUSE_PG_DIST_STATUS to decide: that
bit also reads 0 for a gate that is merely powered off, and an earlier
attempt that skipped on it also skipped the real PW_3/PW_4, lost display
power and blacked the screen.
---
 .../i915/display/intel_display_power_well.c   | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_power_well.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_power_well.c
index 04bd0dd..4aefd1f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_power_well.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_display_power_well.c
@@ -357,6 +357,27 @@ static void hsw_wait_for_power_well_enable(struct intel_display *display,
 	/* Timeout for PW1:10 us, AUX:not specified, other PWs:20 us. */
 	if (intel_de_wait_for_set_ms(display, regs->driver,
 				     HSW_PWR_WELL_CTL_STATE(pw_idx), timeout)) {
+		u32 ctl = intel_de_read(display, regs->driver);
+
+		/*
+		 * Distinguish a real timeout from a power gate that does not
+		 * exist on this SKU. On Lakefield PW_2 never accepts its enable
+		 * request: HSW_PWR_WELL_CTL_REQ() reads back 0 immediately after
+		 * the write, while the other wells set REQ and STATE. A gate the
+		 * hardware refuses to even request is absent, and warning about
+		 * it only produces noise.
+		 *
+		 * Do not use SKL_FUSE_PG_DIST_STATUS for this test: it also reads
+		 * 0 for a gate that is merely powered off, and skipping on it
+		 * skipped the real PW_3/PW_4 and left the display unpowered.
+		 */
+		if (!(ctl & HSW_PWR_WELL_CTL_REQ(pw_idx))) {
+			drm_dbg_kms(display->drm,
+				    "%s: enable request not accepted, gate absent on this SKU\n",
+				    intel_power_well_name(power_well));
+			return;
+		}
+
 		drm_dbg_kms(display->drm, "%s power well enable timeout\n",
 			    intel_power_well_name(power_well));
 
